7 class, committed to Miami on Thursday hours after pulling his commitment from Ohio State.","published":"2026-11-26T22:58:35.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50606746/top-de-recruit-dj-jacobs-commits-miami-hours-decommitting-ohio-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"D.J. Jacobs decommits from Ohio State, sources say, making top DE available again","description":"D.J. Jacobs, the No. 2 overall recruit in the 2027 class, has decommitted from Ohio State, sources told ESPN, with Tennessee, Georgia and Miami among the leading contenders for the five-star defensive end.","published":"2026-11-26T21:21:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50606035/sources-de-dj-jacobs-decommits-ohio-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Friday Night Lights,' 'Ted Lasso' top poll ranking 21st-century sports shows","description":"A Seton Hall poll crowns America's favorite modern fictional sports TV series.﻿","published":"2026-11-26T16:01:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50576889/top-fictional-sports-series-21st-century","type":"Story","byline":"Brianna Williams","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"The oldest grudge in football","description":"When Texas Tech and its brash benefactor bought their way into the college football big time, they were settling an old West Texas score.","published":"2026-11-26T13:12:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50427039/texas-tech-puf-cody-campbell","type":"Story","byline":"Dave Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Take a 360-degree look at college football's iconic rivalry trophies","description":"Whether ancient, animal or absurd, college football's rivalry trophies take many shapes.","published":"2026-11-26T13:09:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/id/50371090/college-football-rivalry-trophies","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"USC band won't perform at UCLA football game after members vandalized campus","description":"The USC Trojan Marching Band will not perform during Saturday's rivalry game against UCLA after members of the band vandalized a portion of UCLA's campus.","published":"2026-11-26T14:39:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50600615/usc-band-perform-members-vandalized-ucla-campus","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Kent State TD overturned by replay was incorrect decision, MAC says","description":"A Kent State touchdown catch should not have been overturned by replay to incomplete at the end of Tuesday's 17-12 loss to Eastern Michigan, the Mid-American Conference said Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T23:05:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50597875/kent-state-td-overturned-replay-was-incorrect-mac-says","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5145410/chris-cole","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)"},"pick":{"pick":8,"round":1,"team":"NO","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Chris Cole (linebacker)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-26T23:15:22Z","intro":"Christopher Cole (born October 3, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the Georgia Bulldogs.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Cole attended Salem High School in Salem, Virginia. As a junior, he recorded 76 tackles and 11 tackles-for-loss. A four-star recruit and one of the top-rated players in the state of Virginia, Cole committed to play college football at the University of Georgia over offers from Miami, Penn State, and Tennessee."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman, Cole totaled 16 tackles and two fumble recoveries, being named to the SEC All-Freshman Team. Entering the 2025 season, he was expected to earn a bigger role in the Bulldogs defense. Cole finished the season recording 60 tackles and 4.5 sacks.Against Oklahoma in 2026, he recorded a sack and two fumble recoveries, returning one 85 yards for a touchdown in a 41–13 victory. Cole was named SEC Defensive Player of the Week for his performance. He was named a Butkus Award semifinalist in October."}]}}